Subject: nvmet: strip the model string before comparing and writing attr_model

On a chassis where dmidecode reports an empty system-product-name, the
middleware's subsys.model() falls through to

    return f'TrueNAS {system_product}'[:MAX_MODEL_LEN]

and builds 'TrueNAS ' -- with a trailing space. update_attrs() reads the
current value back with

    curval = p.read_text().strip()          # kernel.py, ~line 102

so the value it compares against is 'TrueNAS', while the value it wants to
write is 'TrueNAS '. They never match, so every render attempts to rewrite
attr_model. The kernel refuses that write once any host has discovered the
subsystem:

    nvmet: Can't set model number. TrueNAS  is already assigned

which surfaces as EIO. The exception aborts the remainder of the render, so
the namespaces and allowed_hosts symlinks queued behind it never reach the
kernel: the subsystem stays visible but exports nothing, and newly created
namespaces are recorded in the middleware database yet never published.

Stripping the desired value makes it equal the stripped value that is read
back, so the comparison matches and no write is attempted. The stale
'TrueNAS ' already in configfs is left alone -- it is cosmetic, and the
kernel would refuse to change it anyway.

Upstream: NAS-140266 (fixed in TrueNAS 26 BETA).
Applies to: TrueNAS 25.10.x, file
  /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/middlewared/plugins/nvmet/kernel.py

--- a/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/middlewared/plugins/nvmet/kernel.py
+++ b/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/middlewared/plugins/nvmet/kernel.py
@@ -403,7 +403,16 @@
             case 'B':
                 result['attr_cntlid_min'] = 32000
 
-        result['attr_model'] = render_ctx['nvmet.subsys.model']
+        # IDK, 2026-08-17: strip before comparing and writing. dmidecode reports
+        # an empty system-product-name on this chassis, so model() builds
+        # 'TrueNAS ' with a trailing space. configfs reads attr_model back
+        # stripped, so values_match() never matches and update_attrs() rewrites
+        # attr_model on every render. The kernel refuses that write once a host
+        # has discovered the subsystem - 'Can't set model number. TrueNAS  is
+        # already assigned', EIO - and the exception aborts the remainder of the
+        # render, so namespaces and allowed_hosts never reach the kernel.
+        # Upstream fix: NAS-140266.
+        result['attr_model'] = render_ctx['nvmet.subsys.model'].strip()
         result['attr_firmware'] = render_ctx['nvmet.subsys.firmware']
         return result
 
